{
  "configuration_id": "config_041",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_017 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) is the current best at 0.725 acc / 0.685 F1 (3.60 GPU hrs). config_027 (scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) scored 0.713 acc but notably higher F1 (0.695) at 6.22 GPU hrs, suggesting resnet50 features complement the classifier well. Fusion choice (weighted vs concat) showed only a 0.004 gap with imagenet_vit_l (0.725 vs 0.721), so the interaction between resnet50 and concat fusion is untested and could shift the balance. Question: Does scvi_n200 + resnet50 + transformer + concat (config_041) beat the current best 0.725? This is the most logical single extension of the top-2 configurations, combining the strongest RNA encoder and aggregation with the only untested image-encoder/fusion pairing in that neighborhood. With 2 experiments remaining after this, confirming or slightly improving on 0.725 is the highest-value use of the next slot. Expected cost: ~6 GPU hours (similar to config_027, same resnet50 + transformer + multiprofile architecture), which is higher than the imagenet_vit_l variants (~3.6–4.8 hrs) but justified since resnet50 has already shown competitive accuracy and the best-F1 signal."
}

